    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e8f8b29e_afa06d82",
        "filename": "core/api/current.txt",
        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 24879,
      "author": {
        "id": 1074459
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-01-20T20:04:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmm. i\u0027m ok with removing this. But, I do feel like a lot of apps are still using the getNetworkCapabilities API. So, I think we will inevitably get this request somewhere down the line.",
      "parentUuid": "8b30cda0_12d3b66e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 24879,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 24879,
        "endChar": 215
      },
      "revId": "dcb2af16668857d3349753ce7a7a27d7d1d7f58c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c63f6244_3cbfc15d",
        "filename": "core/api/current.txt",
        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 24953,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-01-20T11:57:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do we need to say this, or is it fine to just say INCLUDE_LOCATION_SENSITIVE_INFORMATION ?\nISTM that if the goal is to say this is about being blamed or not blamed, we should simply apply the flag across the board (including for the owner UID in NetworkCapabilities for example which you patch already seems to do, or the location sensitive fields in LinkProperties.).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 24953,
        "startChar": 61,
        "endLine": 24953,
        "endChar": 78
      },
      "revId": "dcb2af16668857d3349753ce7a7a27d7d1d7f58c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "85e8da92_e3f90a0a",
        "filename": "core/api/current.txt",
        "patchSetId": 17
      },
      "lineNbr": 24953,
      "author": {
        "id": 1074459
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-01-20T20:04:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We did discuss this over email. I did consider doing that. But, we run into a backward compatibility issue for existing fields. I\u0027m proposing that we strip out the location sensitive info by default in TransportInfo because we don\u0027t existing apps being blamed for access to WifiInfo fields when they file a default network request or TRANSPORT_WIFI request. So, if we extend that default to existing fields, then we will end up stripping out the existing fields as well when existing apps file their request with no callback flags. So, apps relying on those fields in older SDK\u0027s will suddenly not get that data which will break backwards compatibility. That is the reason I narrowed the scope to just the new location sensitive TransportInfo.\n\nAlso, existing fields that are location sensitive that you pointed out are not currently causing location blame for regular apps:\n\n* OwnerUid in NetworkCapabilities - I\u0027m not gating that field using this flag. Also, the existing logic is to enforce location permission on this field only when sent out to owner app. So, regular apps on the device are not blamed for location access for this field.\nReference: https://source.corp.google.com/android/frameworks/base/services/core/java/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java;l\u003d1714\n\n* LinkProperties: I think location sensitive fields in LinkProperties are only being sent to apps with `NETWORK_SETTINGS` permission. So, regular apps on the device are not blamed for location access for this field (\u0026 do not get these fields).\nReference: https://source.corp.google.com/android/frameworks/base/services/core/java/com/android/server/ConnectivityService.java;rcl\u003d0675a4acb6889b46317944d771f5753385c1521b;l\u003d1744",
      "parentUuid": "c63f6244_3cbfc15d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 24953,
        "startChar": 61,
        "endLine": 24953,
        "endChar": 78
      },
      "revId": "dcb2af16668857d3349753ce7a7a27d7d1d7f58c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
